        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS ot the Peace LO r the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be holden at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, in and for the said County, on "NIDaY, the 26`h day of June next, at half-nest eleven clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand jury will be tna,Pannelled. rltle hearine of all appeals arising within the Hundreds Broxton, Edd,sbury, Nantwich, and Wirral, farming to.e Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners corn- from such Hundreds, will take place at such Sea- 9s. The Grand and Petty Juriee for the Chester Die- • must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the openin, of the Court on MONDAY, the 26:n day of aSine next, at half-past eleven o'clock in the Forenoon- ir THE Court will be Adjourned to the Court House, -&gt;nutsford, on WEDNESDAY, the 25th day of June next, at eleven o'clock in the forenoon, when another Grand Ja.rY will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals 4rlsing within the Hundreds of Bucklow, Macclesfield, and Northwich, forming the Bnutsford District, air `43 trials of Rll prisoners committed from tbe last men Hundreds will take place at such Ad' .!!ssions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the F vistrict must be in attendance at the Coy Xnutsford, at the opening of the Court on V ti"l 28th day of June next, at eleven o' Forenoon.</p>
        <p>REGINALD Pc,. Clerk of the Peace fnr the County of Chester. Chaster, 6th June, 1699.</p>
