      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0073" n="art0073">
        <p>RESULTS OF BOOTS, CASH CHEMISTS,</p>
        <p>SPRING CLEANING CO NIPETITIONS</p>
        <p>(ScuooL PRizEs). ENGLISH COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>For the two best compositions on Spring Cleaning, written by any pupil mnder 18 years of age and attPn4ing an 7 Ele- mentary Public School or Continuation School. E, has been awarded to GEORGE LA3IB of Hatfield- road Board Salo )1, St. Albans. Age oi Competitor 9. Standard 5.</p>
        <p>2Q has been awarded to SANE F. BULL of 'the National Mixed School, Leamingt oil Spa. Age of Competitor 13. Standard 6.</p>
        <p>ENGLISH COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>For the two best letters on Spring Cleaning sent in by a pupil not higher than the 4th Standard in any Illementary Public School-</p>
        <p>243 e.) has been awarded to ELLEN SHARP of the Garden Fields Board School, St. Albans, Herts. Age of Competitor 11. Standard 4. bas been awarded to CONSTANCE ELLA. DAVIS a of Bedford-road Board School, Bootle, Liverpool. Age of Competitor 9. Standard 2. FRENCH AND GERMAN COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Whilst competitons freely came in for the English corn- Position prizes, those in French or German were very small in number, and for the most part poor in quality. The competitions were advertised over a very wide area-85 towns—in addition to such large cities as Manchester, Liver- pool, Birmingham, &amp;a_ having altogether a total population of many millions. The only one sent in from a Board School was receivedlfrom a pupil of Huntingden-street Board School, Nottingham. Comparing the number of replies received for various English competitions and those for competitions in. French or Germrn, it would appear that a most unsatis- factory percentage of the pupils even in the highest standards of the Board and National Schools have any practical knowledge whatever of French or German. 25 has been awarded to MARY ELIZABETH LAWSON, Huntiagton-street Board School, Nottingham, for a letter in French. Age of Competitor 16. We are unable to award the second and third prizes in connection with this competition. FRENCH AND GERMAN COMPETITIONS.-</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0074" n="art0074">
