        <p>• GREAT CLEARANCE SALE AT PIT TS 'S, LONDON-ROAD, MANG El EST ER. Just Past Station. Through Railway Arch. THE LARGEST AND MOST CONVENIENT GENERAL FURNISHING ESTABLISHMENT IN THE KINGDOM. Electric Lighted Throughout. Passenger Lifts To All Floors "IN THE SPRING TIME A YOUNG MAN'S FANCY LIGHTLY TURNS TO THOUGHTS OF LOVE," and having fortunately obtained his financee's con- sent to marriage, the important question, "Where shall we Furnish ?" presents itself. Both the young people have been very forcibly impressed by the magnificent display in PITTS'S Colossal Showrooms, together with the genuine ring In PITTS'S Advertisaments and the uniformly good reputa- tion PITTS'S bear, but before definitely decidi3g they very wisely concluded to refer the matter to their parents' suporior judgment and experence. Upon broaching the subject the unhesitating reply is "CERTAINLY FURNISH AT PITTS'S, like we did nearly thirty years ago. You see the goods are little wcrae for wear after all these years. PITTS'S eccupy the uncommon position of often having furnished three consecutive generations, parents, children and grand- children, and you cannot possibly do better than place the order with that old-established firm." Result, another home made bright and comfortable at little cost by PITTb'S to the great satisfaction of all concerned. PITTS'S GREAT CLEARANCE SALE.—HOUSES OF FURNITURE at 15k, 22i. 281, 34, 50, 75, 100. 200, up to 1.0:0 guineas, combining the maximum of good taste and durability with minimum cost. These easily surpass and excel all others. their praises having been extolled in HUNDREDS OF UNSOLICITED TESTIMONIALS and PRESS NOTICES. They challenge the most critical judg- ment, and are considered by connoisseurs to be WORTH DOUBLE THE PRICE ASKED. Full particulars, together with NEW ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUIDE. con- taining 700 designs, and showing HOW TO SAVE 25 to 60 per cent, sent post free. Cash Prices only quoted. Deferred Payments arranged. PITTS'S GREAT CLEARANCE SALE,—COM- PLETE HOUSE OF FURNITURE for 221 guineas, equal to what expensive City firms charge £4O for, contains: —Artistie SITTING-ROOM Suite in Leather, consisting of tasteful Couch or Sofa, Pair of Easy Chairs and Set of Small Chairs, substantial Dining Table, Carpet or Floorcloth. nice design, Hearth Rug, Brass Bar, Fender and Set of Brasses. Cornice Pole, and Pair of Curtains. KITCHEN has strong Dresser, Set of Chairs, Rocking and Arm Chairs, sound square or fall leaf Table, Fender. Fire Irons. Floorcloth, and Rug. BEDROOM : Serviceable Suite, polished or enamelled, Cane Chairs, Towel Rail, Toilet Service, strong full-sized Bedstead, Wire Spring Mattress, Wool Overlay, Bolster and two Pillows, Carpet or Floorcloth, and Fender. HALL, STAIRS, and LANDING: Carpet. Floorcloth, stair Rods an d Eyes, Brass Door /Plate, Cocoa and Door Mats. The most marvellous value obtainable. PITTS'S GREAT CLEARANCE SALE.—ENTIRE CONTENTS OF SEVEN-ROOMED HOUSE, origin- ally cost £lBo,for 75 guineas. The Dining-room is in morocco leather, the Drawing-room is in Rosewood, a spare room up- stairs, fitted as a smokerocen, is in Sandlebags. Furniture complete for Kitchen, Hall, Stairs, Landing, Cellars. &amp;c. The First Bedroom is in American Walnut. including Wardrobe, Dressing Table, Washstand, Chairs, &amp;c.. Bedsteads, Bedding Carpet, Rug. and Toilet Service. The Second Bedroom is in Asm and the rhird Bedroom is in Mahogany. Undoubtedly the greatest bargain ever offered. PITTS'S FOR CARPftTS AND FLOOR COVER- INGS. All British make. Fitted free. Largest, best, and cheapest stock. Astounding value. Grand display. Well worth inspection. pITTS'S BASSINETrES, Lamps, China, Glass, Earthenware, Pianos, Cycles. Magnificent display in Show Windows. Pleasure to see it. PITTS'S FOR OFFICE AND LIBRARY FURNITURE. EVERY DESCRIPTION OF BOOK- CASES, Secretaries. Desks, Stools. Chairs, Safes, Copying Presses, at about half City Prices. SAMUEL PITTS, Established 1845 LONDON ROAD (just pas