        <p>TE PUBLIC HEALTH ACT, 1875.-THE RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL OF RUNCORN—The Contributory Places of HelsbY, Grappenhall, Latchford (Without), and Walton Inferior. NOTICR IS HRRHBY GIVRN, that under the provi- sions of the Public Health Act, 1875, Bye-Laws have been made by the Rural District Council of Runcorn, for the above mentioned Contributory elaces, and such Bye-laws will be submitted to the Local Glovernmeat Board for confir- mation immediately after the 12th DAY of JULY, 1839, and Notice is hereby further given, that a copy of such B ye-Laws will be kept 'at 71, High-street, Runcorn, the Office of the Rural District Council of Runcorn. for one Calendar month, from the 10th DAY of JUNR. 1899, and will be op,m during office hours at the said office, to the inspection of the Rate- payers of the District, to which such Bye-Laws relate, with- out fee or reward. Dated this Bth day of June. 1899. C-HORGE F. ASHTON. Acting Clerk of the Rural District Council of Runcorn. 71, High-street, Runcorn.</p>
