        <p>EXHIBITION OF MODERN LITHOGRAPHS AT THE MUSEUM. --- Thera is now on view at the Warrington Museum a collection of modern lithographs, about one hundred an number, lent by Mr. Charles Holine, the editor of the "Studio." The exhibition should be visited by all in- terested in artistic work, tor it enables the visi- tor to appreciate the modern revival of the neg- lected arc of lithography. The present collection clonsists of representative examples of recent work by British and Continental artistes, and were included in the recent exhibition of lithographs at South Kensing- ton, to commemorate the discovery of the process by Senetelder, in 1798. By far the most notable feature of that exhibition consisted of the distinctive and character- istic examples of the modern dchool of "Auto-litho- graphy." In the early days of lithography it was the tci o regard the art as merely method of repro- dfauschtiioonn , and a tithographic copy of a painting, that was made to appear as much as possible like an engraving or mezzotint, was the most acceptable expression of the craft that could be found. In the middle of this century a decline set in, acd in the sixties and seventies litho- graphy became little more than a purely commercial process. During the last decade, however, a strong revival has taken place, and the work now being exceuped promises to 'supersede in artistic interest all that of former times. Artists of well-known ability have turned their attention to the discovery of new possibilities, and, under their fostering care, the lithe- graph has been rescued from the banalties of pure com- mercialism, and raised to the rank of a fine art. Whislter Shaonon, and Pennell, in England; Steinlau. Fantle-Latour and Riy:ere, in France ;' Thome. Greiner and Sterl in Germany ; aucl many others of scarcely lees ability, are responsible for examples of great artistic value, which sre, and will continue to be, treasured by the connoisseur as they deserve. Some of the work of tbe artists mentioned are included in the present collec- tion. •</p>
