        <p>THE TRANSVAAL CONFERENCE. KRUGER AND MILNER FAIL TO AGREE. MATJESFONTEINT, THURSDAY, The conference between Presid-at Kruger and Sir A. Milner has failed. It dealt chiefly witto the franchise question. Sir A Milner proposei that all foreigners should receive the full francnise after fivo years' reel dance with retrospective effeet, and on making a simpl oath of allegiance. The ugh Commissioner also pro- pesed that there should be some additional seats for the Rand. A RECORD RAILWAY RUN. LONDON TO CREWE IN THREE HOURS. Over one hundred members of the Institution of Civil Engineers visited Crewe works yesterday afternoon. The party left Euston in a special train at ten, and reached Crewe, 158 miles, in three hours a record run. dyneometer car was attached to the train to record - Ithe speed. At Crewe the Engineers inspected the work- shops, and also a new system of points and signals worked by electricity. SUICIDE IN GAOL. A convict, Henry Taylor, committed suicide by hang- ing in his cell at Parkhurst Prison, Isle of Wight, yestere day. A TRAIN STRUCK BY LIGHTNING. NEW YORK, THURSDAY. A car containing oil was struck by lightning on Wed- nesday as a train was passing over a bridge in Holly (Michigan). A terrific explosion ensued which sotne pletely destroyed the bridge and nine cars- Five per- sons are missing. TRAIN ROBBERS AT BAY. A SHERIFF KILLED. NEW YORK, THURSDAY. Further advices received here regarding the attack made upon the overland train on the Union Pacific line near Wilcox, Wyoming, on the 2nd inst., state that three of the robbers. on being surrounded by the posse despatched against them, fired and killed the sheriff. RESIGN A.TION OF A NORT.HWICH CONGREGATIONAL MINISTER. Much astonishm-mt and regret were caused in North wide yesterday, by the intimation that the Rev. Frederick Carter, secretary of the Cheshire Congrega- tional Union, has tendered Ws resi4na-ion as Pastor of Northwich Congregational Church. He has held the position twenty years, and has been identified with the erection of new local Coneregational buildings costing £6,000. The reason assigned tor the resignation is that the Congregational Union have earnestly requested him to accept a pastorate at Knutsford, and to take charge of otherimportant Cheshire Union work. LATEST LOCAL WEA.THEIt FORECAST. Tne following forecast of the weather fe. the ensuing twenty-feur hours in the north-west of Eaeland (includ- , jag Manchester, Liverpool, and Holyheed) was issued at the Meteorological Office at three o'clock yesterday afternoon : Easterly and North-easterly winds, moderate ; fine generally. YESTERDAY'S CRICKET. The following are the scores at close of play in the first-class cricket matches played yesterday: LANCASHIRE v. SURREY.—Lancashire, all 0ut,262. Surrey, 73 for 2 ; Abel. not out 28 ; Jephson not out, 34. MIDDLESEX V. SUSSEX : Sussex, 378 for 9. KENT v• SOMERSETSHIRE :—KenC, 325 ; Somerset 67 for none. ESSEX v. HAMPSHIRE :—Hampshire all out, 166. CAMBRIDGE UNIVERSITY v. THE AUSTRA- LIANS :—Carnbridge. 397 for 7. YORKSHIRE v. DERBYSHIRE :—Yorkshire, all out 343, Derbyshire 36 for 1. GLOUCESTERSHIRE v. NOTTS :—Notts 438 for 2; Jo nes made 250, and Shrewsbury 146..</p>
